Theorem L-9: SCALAR sentinel excluded from lattice operations

  Preconditions:
    - SCALAR is the scalar sentinel per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-9
    - SCALAR is NOT a lattice element (not in any per-dimension carrier)
    - Per Appendix A: SCALAR is emitted by TF-1 (Let { Literal }), TF-2a
      (Let { PrimOp }), TF-10 (IsShared), TF-10a (Reset)
    - Per sec-3 TF-8 (Select): when one operand is SCALAR, the rule
      pre-filters SCALAR before invoking join (i.e. join is NEVER called
      on a SCALAR operand)

  Soundness property:
    Forall a in AimsState. join(a, SCALAR) is undefined.
    Analysis SHALL exclude scalars from the state map.
    TF-8 (Select) excludes SCALAR operand BEFORE join (pre-filter, not
    lattice join with SCALAR).

  Proof obligation:
    Two-part discharge:
      (a) SCALAR is not in any per-dimension carrier; join is total only
          over the carrier product; therefore join(a, SCALAR) is
          definitionally outside the join's domain.
      (b) Every TF-N call site that could pair a SCALAR with a non-SCALAR
          state pre-filters SCALAR before invoking join.

    Part (a) — domain enumeration:
      Per-dimension carriers (per Annex E §AIMS §3.1 through §AIMS §3.7):
        Access = {B, O} — SCALAR not in
        Consumption = {empty, L, A, U} — SCALAR not in
        Cardinality = {absent, 1, omega} — SCALAR not in
        Uniqueness = {u, ms, s} — SCALAR not in
        Locality = {bl, fl, ae, he, top} — SCALAR not in
        Shape = {Phi, R_S, R_V, C, H} — SCALAR not in
        Effect = 3-bit flag set — SCALAR not in

      Total carrier-product domain: 2 * 4 * 3 * 3 * 5 * 5 * 8 = 14,400
      states. SCALAR is not any of them. Per-dimension membership
      enumeration: 30 element checks across the 7 carriers, each
      confirming SCALAR not equal to any value.

    Part (b) — pre-filter enumeration at TF-N call sites:
      Appendix A enumerates TF-1 / TF-2a / TF-10 / TF-10a as the only
      SCALAR producers. TF-8 (Select) is the only join site that can
      receive a SCALAR operand (because Select's operands are
      arbitrary previously-defined variables). Per sec-3 TF-8 spec:
        - both SCALAR -> dst := SCALAR; no join.
        - one SCALAR -> exclude SCALAR; dst inherits non-SCALAR with
          uniqueness := max(MaybeShared, non_scalar.uniqueness)
          (downgrade ensures monotonicity per L-6).
        - neither SCALAR -> standard join.
      In NO case does join receive a SCALAR operand. The TF-11
      backward-demand discipline mirrors this: TF-11 emits Once-demand
      on operands; SCALAR operands generate no RC demand (per
      DP-1 is_rc_needed = false on is_scalar()).

    Pipeline-level enforcement per sec-6 IA-8:
      Variables carrying the logical Immortal classification and SCALAR
      variables are excluded from the AimsStateMap. The map's
      key set is a subset of non-SCALAR, non-immortal ArcVarId
      indices, so every map entry's value is in the carrier domain
      defined in Part (a).

    SCALAR semantics summary:
      - SCALAR is a TF-output marker, NOT a join input
      - canonicalize MUST NOT propagate SCALAR (Appendix B / sec-2)
      - the state map's keys are filtered to non-SCALAR vars per IA-8
      - L-9 holds by construction: the join function's domain is the
        carrier product, which excludes SCALAR

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension carrier-membership enumeration + TF-8
        pre-filter enumeration per section_02::verify_l9_scalar_exclusion)
      monotonicity (validates TF-8 SCALAR-pre-filter downgrade
        preserves monotonicity per the L-6 specification)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-9 via carrier-membership enumeration + TF-8 pre-filter call-site enumeration
